  (text "EN: R201 10k pull-up + C204 100nF, U202 TPS3808G33 (3.07 V, open drain, 20 ms with CT open) drives CHIP_PU. SW201 RESET removed per rework 2026-10-18.\nBOOT: GPIO0 R202 10k pull-up to +3V3. SW202 BOOT removed per rework 2026-10-18. Straps GPIO3/45/46 isolated (no-connect); GPIO35/36/37 octal PSRAM, no-connect.\nUSB-C J201 data only: CC1/CC2 separate 5.1k, U203 ESD, 22R series to GPIO19/20; VBUS feeds U203 pin 5 and C205 only (board powered from the battery).\nProgramming and serial debug use native USB (J201 USB-C USB_Serial_JTAG with built-in auto-reset/auto-download).\nUART0 header J202, R207, R211 removed per rework 2026-10-18; TXD0 (IO43), RXD0 (IO44), IO2, IO6 are no-connect."
    (at 25.4 26.67 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid "c347af4d-cbc3-46d9-87cb-21ef4d6f1a52")
  )
  (text "Pin map (battery-monitor-rev-a, reworked 2026-10-18): IO8 I2C_SDA, IO9 I2C_SCL (on-board ADS1115 0x48), IO5 BTN_USER (J504 external button), IO38 GAUGE_EN (LED voltmeter switch on 05-io),\nIO40 LED_STATUS, IO41 LED_ALERT, LoRa IO10-15/21 as rev-c. Programming/debug: native USB (USB_Serial_JTAG on J201; SW201, SW202, J202 removed).\nIO4 no-connect: divider always on, about 0.1 mA (was SENSE_EN). IO1 no-connect. IO7 no-connect (ADS1115 ALERT/RDY not used, firmware polls).\nIO2, IO6, TXD0 (IO43), RXD0 (IO44) no-connect (J202 and J502 removed). Free (no-connect): IO1/2/4/6/7/16/17/18/39/42/43/44/47/48.\nU201 BOM: ESP32-S3-WROOM-1-N16R8 from owner stock, or N16/N8 (same footprint; PSRAM not used by the firmware)."
    (at 25.4 279.4 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid "48c917f8-3487-4785-8a83-f57fbe76ead7")
  )
